  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a contributor, I want `ForumSessionCheckTests` to pass reliably on the iOS simulator CI, so that unrelated PRs are not blocked by a red `App build + tests` job.\n\n### Observed\n\nTwo failures in two days on PRs that do not touch `App/` or the code under test (both tests use `ScriptedRefresher`, never `SessionRefreshFlow`); a rerun of the failed job passed the first time:\n\n- #356 (LOT-057, HFRKit REST only), run 41232795746: `ForumSessionCheckTests/loginSavedWhileACheckWritesBackWinsOverItsCookies()` failed at its 60 s `.timeLimit`.\n- #364 (#320, HFRKit session probe), run 41323654034: `ForumSessionCheckTests.loginDuringARecheckWinsOverItsResult()` failed.\n\nBoth tests drive a re-check and a login concurrently through gates (`CheckGate`, `beforePersistWrite`) under `.timeLimit(.minutes(1))` (`App/SwiftHFRTests/Accounts/ForumSessionCheckTests.swift:184-232`).\n\n### Scope\n\nFind why they can hang or fail on a loaded simulator runner (a gate never entered, an ordering the test assumes, the time limit itself) and make them deterministic. Not a guess: reproduce first (e.g. repeated runs of the suite on the simulator), then fix the test or the model.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Root cause stated on this issue with evidence (a reproduction or a trace).\n- [ ] Both tests deterministic; the suite passes N repeated runs on the simulator (N stated).\n- [ ] `App build + tests` green.\n",
