   "created_at": "2026-11-02T00:08:28Z",
   "updated_at": "2026-11-02T00:08:28Z",
   "body": "Root cause: the `.timeLimit(.minutes(1))` measured main-actor queueing, not the tests themselves. On the CI runner, untimed app tests report 30–120 s for milliseconds of work: in run 41232795746, other suites passed at 119.9 s while the timed test failed at 60.000 s. When the limit fires, Xcode kills the runner, so the second log has no result line for it. Reproduced locally by holding the main actor for 65 s in a throwaway test: a timed test failed at 60.000 s with 'exceeded execution time allowance'. In isolation, the suite passed 500/500 under CPU load, so there is no model race. Fix in #385: the gate fails fast with `finish()`/`#require(entered())` and the time limits are removed. Repeat counts are in the PR.",
   "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
